                content: `
                    <p>Over 80% of men experience noticeable hair thinning by age 50. In the overwhelming majority of cases, the culprit is <strong>Androgenetic Alopecia (AGA)</strong>. Testosterone in the scalp is converted by the 5-alpha reductase enzyme into <strong>Dihydrotestosterone (DHT)</strong>, which shrinks vulnerable hair follicles until they can no longer produce visible terminal hairs.</p>

                    <div class="quick-verdict">
                        <h3>⚡ Executive Summary</h3>
                        <p>Do not wait for noticeable scalp shine before taking action. Combining active DHT-reducing cleansers with scalp circulation massage and lightweight matte fibers (like <strong>American Crew Fiber</strong>) protects follicles while restoring instant volume.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Three Clinically Proven Pillars for Regrowth</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Inhibit Follicle Miniaturization:</strong> Wash with ketoconazole, saw palmetto, or caffeine-infused shampoos 3x weekly to cleanse sebum and surface DHT.</li>
                        <li><strong>Stimulate Scalp Microcirculation:</strong> Perform 4 minutes of firm mechanical scalp massage daily to oxygenate follicle roots.</li>
                        <li><strong>Avoid Heavy Pore-Clogging Products:</strong> Use water-based matte styling products that rinse out cleanly without residue.</li>
