                image: "images/article3.jpg",
                author: "HaircutZonePro Lab",
                date: "Updated Oct 2025",
                rating: "9.7/10",
                content: `
                    <p>Walk down any grooming aisle and you will find clays, pastes, pomades, waxes, fibers, and creams. Choosing the wrong one leaves your hair looking like an oil slick or a dried brick. Here is the definitive barber guide:</p>

                    <h3>1. Hair Clay & Fiber (Best for Modern Textured Looks)</h3>
                    <p>Contains natural bentonite or kaolin clay. Absorbs excess sebum, provides a pliable high hold, and delivers a natural 100% matte finish. Ideal for short to medium haircuts and thinning hair.</p>

                    <h3>2. Water-Based Pomade (Best for Slick Backs & Side Parts)</h3>
                    <p>Provides a clean sheen and crisp comb lines. Unlike old-school oil-based grease pomades, water-based formulations wash out effortlessly in one warm rinse.</p>

                    <h3>3. Styling Wax (Best for Spiky & Edgy Styles)</h3>
                    <p>Delivers firm hold with moderate pliability for messy textured hairstyles.</p>

                    <div class="product-callout">
